DENG-730: raw MessagePack slices inside tracked containers.
Pinned DIDE protocol 1.9-67d655e06fe7 (MPack 1.1.1, MIT).

MPack reader_remaining() asserts that every compound is closed. Generated raw
fields are decoded inside maps, so Debug builds abort despite valid input.
Borrow the exposed cursor of the pinned immutable-data reader around the
unchanged mpack_discard validation. Reject mutable/refill/skip readers and clear
failed outputs. No protocol bytes, API, archive pin or tracking flag changes.

Local patch only; no upstream report per DENG-2. Re-check/drop if a future pinned
protocol generator implements the equivalent contiguous-reader contract.

--- a/de_editor_protocol.c
+++ b/de_editor_protocol.c
@@ -98,8 +98,16 @@
 static void de_ep_read_raw(mpack_reader_t *r, de_ep_raw *out) {
-    const char *start = NULL, *end = NULL;
-    mpack_reader_remaining(r, &start);
+    memset(out, 0, sizeof(*out));
+    /* Raw views borrow the immutable frame. Buffered/refill readers cannot keep
+     * those views alive; reader_remaining() also requires all maps to be closed. */
+    if (r->buffer || r->fill || r->skip) {
+        mpack_reader_flag_error(r, mpack_error_unsupported);
+        return;
+    }
+    const char *start = r->data;
     mpack_discard(r);
-    mpack_reader_remaining(r, &end);
-    out->ptr = start;
-    out->len = (start && end && end >= start) ? (size_t)(end - start) : 0;
+    const char *end = r->data;
+    if (mpack_reader_error(r) == mpack_ok && start && end && end > start) {
+        out->ptr = start;
+        out->len = (size_t)(end - start);
+    }
 }
